\section{Experimental details}
\label{app:details}

\paragraph{E1 (development set).}
The race grid crosses $\lambda\in\{\EoneLamValues\}$, $p_0\in\{\EonePzeroValues\}$, $\alpha\in\{\EoneAlphaValues\}$ and $a_0\in\{10^{-4},10^{-2}\}$ with \EoneSeeds{} seeds; two further grids vary $\kappa$ and the depth $L$.
The rank is read at $T=\min(1.3\,t_{\mathrm{race}}+300,\EoneHorizon)$, so E1 measures agreement with the rank \emph{at} $T$, which can still change where the race is unfinished or $\lambda=0$.
Orthogonal initialisation uses $d=32$ and orthogonal encoder columns of norms $a_0e^{0.1\xi_k}$, $\xi_k\sim\mathcal N(0,1)$; Gaussian initialisation uses entries of variance $a_0^2/n$ with $d=32$ or $d=128$, and the criterion then uses each direction's initial norm $\|\Wc_0u_k\|$.
A direction counts as surviving if $\|\Wc u_k\|>\EoneSvThr$ at $t=T$.
In \EoneRaceUnfinishedOrth{} of the \EoneRaceRuns{} orthogonal runs of the race grid the horizon \EoneHorizon{} is reached before $1.3\,t_{\mathrm{race}}+300$, and the criterion is evaluated with the same $T$.
The race grid has \EoneRaceRuns{} runs per initialisation; the EMA grid uses the EMA growth rate of \cref{sec:heuristics} and the depth grid an identity-initialised linear predictor of depth $L$.

\paragraph{E1: knobs, EMA and depth.}
With orthogonal initialisation the criterion classifies \EoneModeAccOrth{} of the \EoneModes{} directions and gives the exact rank in \EoneRankExactOrth{} of runs (initial window \EoneWindowExactOrth{}; the static bound over-predicts by \EoneBoundMaeOrth{} in every run; \cref{tab:accuracy}); without weight decay nothing survives at $p_0=1$, and the rank is non-monotone in $\lambda$ and $p_0$.
Gaussian initialisation gives exact rank in \EoneRankExactGauss{} ($d=32$) and \EoneRankExactGaussWide{} ($d=128$) of runs; the exact reduced flow \eqref{eq:reduced} matches gradient descent on every direction, so the error is the near-collapse approximation.
With the EMA rate of \cref{sec:heuristics} the criterion classifies \EoneModeAccEma{} of directions; deeper predictors keep fewer directions, as the clock $L\alpha\lambda_P$ implies, but with exact rank in only \EoneRankExactDepth{} of runs, errors that are almost all false survivals.
At $\lambda=\EoneLamValues$ the measured rank is $\EoneLamRanks$ against the predicted $\EoneLamPred$ and the static $\EoneLamBound$, and at $\lambda=0.01$ the rank over the $p_0$ grid is $\EonePzeroRanks$ (\cref{fig:e1-knobs}).
At $\lambda=0.01$ and $p_0=1$, just above the window of the leading direction, a slower target raises the rank slightly, as predicted for $p_0>p_+^k$ (\cref{fig:e1-knobs}d); the one miss, at $\kappa=0.03$, is where the adiabatic treatment of the EMA, which needs $\kappa\gg\alpha\lambda_P$, is weakest.
At $\lambda=0$ and $p_0=0.5$, inside the window, only the slowest target lowers the rank.
In the depth grid the criterion classifies \EoneModeAccDepth{} of directions, with \EoneModeFalsePosDepth{} false survivals against \EoneModeFalseNegDepth{} missed.

