\paragraph{E1b: further arms.}
On the phase grid at $p_0=0.5$ and $\lambda=\EoneBGridLams$ the rank is $\EoneBGridRanksHalf$ against the predicted $\EoneBGridPredHalf$ (\cref{sec:heldout}).
Finality of the rank (\texttt{results/checks/e1b\_long\_horizon.json}): on the \EoneBLongRuns{} runs with $\lambda>0$ where \cref{prop:reduction} is exact (grid, EMA rate $\times$ predictor learning rate, balanced, depth $1$), the reduced flow run from each run's initial norms reproduces the measured fate of every direction at the end of training in \EoneBLongReproduced{} runs; continued to $2t_{\mathrm{end}}$ and to $t=\EoneBLongT$, \EoneBLongChanged{} runs gain one direction and none loses one, and the exact-rank rate of the race is \EoneBLongExactLong{} against the long-horizon rank and \EoneBLongExactEnd{} against the rank at the end of training. Amplitudes below $10^{-150}$ are flushed to zero in the simulation, as in the measured runs; without this floor a direction can still recover, \EoneBLongChangedNoFloor{} runs gain one direction by $t=\EoneBLongT$, and the exact-rank rate rises to \EoneBLongExactNoFloor{}, because the extra recoveries are directions the race predicted to survive. At $\lambda=0$ the rank is a horizon rank (\EoneBLongZeroChanged{} of the \EoneBLongZeroRuns{} grid runs gain a direction by $t=\EoneBLongT$), and the prediction is the $\lambda_P=0$ branch of \cref{def:race}, which uses $T$.
Tian et al.'s criterion and \cref{cor:alpha1} are exact in \EoneBBalancedExact{} of \EoneBBalancedRuns{} balanced runs.
For random Gaussian predictors the general criterion has error \EoneBRandMae{} and for non-commuting statistics \EoneBNoncommMae{}; \EoneBDiverged{} further runs with two-factor random predictors at $p_0=2$ diverged numerically at step $0.1$; re-run at step \EoneBSmallEta{} (\EoneBSmallEtaStill{} diverge, \texttt{results/checks/e1b\_small\_eta.json}), they leave the general criterion passing on all \EoneBSmallEtaN{} runs, both against the predictions as pre-registered (error \EoneBPreregMae{}, exact rank in \EoneBPreregExact{}; this is the pre-registered test) and with the predictions recomputed at the smaller step (error \EoneBSmallEtaMae{}, exact \EoneBSmallEtaExact{}). On the \EoneBSmallEtaRuns{} re-run runs alone the general criterion fails: error \EoneBRerunPreregMae{} and exact rank in \EoneBRerunPreregExact{} with the predictions as pre-registered, and error \EoneBRerunRecompMae{} with them recomputed.
With finite batches the rank rises with the batch size ($\EoneBBatchHalf$ for $B=8,32,128$ at $p_0=0.5$) towards the population prediction $\EoneBBatchHalfPred$.
Early per-direction log-growth matches the predicted rate with $R^2\ge\EoneBTrajRsq$ for $p_0\le1$ and $\ge\EoneBTrajRsqEma$ with an EMA target; at $p_0=2$ ($R^2=\EoneBTrajRsqBig$) the continuous-time rate is wrong because $\eta|g_k|$ is no longer small, and the per-step rate $\log(1+\eta g_k)/\eta$, a post-hoc diagnostic, gives $R^2\ge\EoneBTrajRsqEuler$.

\paragraph{E1c: held-out test of the depth correction.}
E1c uses statistics not seen before ($n=d=16$, $\sigma_k$ evenly spaced from $2$ to $0.6$, $c_k=0.88^k\sigma_k$) and crosses $L\in\{1,2,3,4\}$, $\lambda\in\{0.003,0.006,0.012,0.024\}$ and $p_0\in\{0.4,0.8,1.2\}$ with 3 seeds (\EoneCRuns{} runs; identity factors, copy target, $\alpha=1$, $a_0=10^{-3}$, gradient descent with step $0.1$).
The predictions of the depth-$L$ and the depth-1 nullcline and \EoneCCritAll{} criteria were committed before any run (\texttt{results/e1c/prediction.json}); both pass.
For $L=2,3,4$ the rank error is $\EoneCMaeByL$ with the depth-$L$ nullcline against $\EoneCMaeOneByL$ with the depth-1 one, and the per-direction accuracy is \EoneCModeAcc{}; the depth-1 rule over-predicts in \EoneCOverOne{} runs, the corrected one never over-predicts and under-predicts in \EoneCUnder{}, \EoneCUnderFour{} of them at $L=4$: it is conservative, most of all at $L=4$, and depth is not fully resolved.
For $L=1$ both rules coincide and are exact; no rank changes between $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ and $2t_{\mathrm{end}}$, and the static bound misses by \EoneCBoundMae{} at every depth.
The test covers identity-initialised factors with aligned statistics only, not random or non-commuting deep predictors.

