\paragraph{E2: masking.}
The data are a Gaussian field on a cycle of $n=d=64$ sites (correlation $0.7^{\mathrm{distance}}$), with context and target complementary under a mask. Cyclic masks (Bernoulli, one block, four blocks) make $\Sigma_c$ and $\Sigma_{tc}$ circulant, so the race applies per frequency; a non-wrapping block needs the general form. The grid crosses $r\in\{0.1,\dots,0.9\}$, four $\lambda$ from $3\cdot10^{-4}$ to $10^{-2}$, $p_0\in\{0.25,0.5\}$ and 3 seeds.
Masks act by zeroing, $x_c=m_c\circ x$ and $x_t=m_t\circ x$, so the population statistics $G_{ij}=\Pr(i,j\in c)$ and $F_{ij}=\Pr(i\in t,j\in c)$ are exact.
Bernoulli masks make each site a target with probability $r$; a block mask takes one cyclic target block of length $\mathrm{round}(rn)$ at a uniform position, the multiblock mask the union of four cyclic blocks of length $\ell\in\{1,2,3,4,6,\dots,14\}$ (nominal $r=4\ell/n$), and the non-wrapping block one block inside $[0,n)$; the context is always the complement.
All arms use $\Pred_0=p_0I$, a copy target with stop-gradient, $\alpha=1$, an orthogonal encoder of scale $a_0=10^{-3}$, weight decay $\lambda$ on every weight and Euler step $0.05$, run to $t_{\mathrm{end}}=\min(3t_{\mathrm{race}}+300,\,4000)$ with $t_{\mathrm{race}}$ the predicted end of the race; ranks count singular values of $\Wc$ above $0.05$.
The SGD (linear encoder), tanh and two-layer arms draw fresh fields and masks in batches of $64$; the tanh encoder is $\tanh(\Wc x)$, predicted by the linear race; the exploratory two-layer encoder is $W_2\tanh(W_1x)$ with $W_1\in\mathbb R^{128\times64}$ at standard scale and $W_2$ near collapse, predicted by the general form on the hidden-feature statistics at initialisation, although $W_1$ trains; the no-predictor arm fixes $\Pred=I$ and measures the growth sign of each frequency, predicted positive iff $c_k-\sigma_k-\lambda>0$, possible because context and target marginals differ (for Bernoulli masks iff $(2r-1)\hat\Sigma_k>2r$ up to $\lambda$; \cref{app:more}).
No run diverged (\EtwoExcluded{} excluded).
Without a predictor, heavy Bernoulli masking makes directions grow wherever this condition predicts it (\EtwoNopredGrowth{} configurations).
Three criteria fail their registered thresholds (\cref{tab:e2}): the peak criterion requires every predicted rise and fall to be measured (\EtwoNonmonoConf{} of \EtwoNonmonoPred{}), and since \EtwoPeakEdge{} of the \EtwoPeakProfiles{} predicted maxima reach the grid edge, it tests non-monotonicity on these Bernoulli profiles only; the tanh arm requires an error of at most $1.5$ and below the static bound (\EtwoTanhMae{} against \EtwoTanhBoundMae{}); and the exploratory two-layer arm at most $2$ and below the bound (\EtwoMlpMae{} against \EtwoMlpBoundMae{}).
Finality and precision (\texttt{results/checks/e2\_long\_horizon.json}): for the \EtwoLongRuns{} cyclic population runs every Fourier column follows the scalar reduced flow of \cref{prop:reduction}, which reproduces the measured rank at $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ in \EtwoLongReproduced{} runs.
The three exceptions (Bernoulli, $r=0.4$, $\lambda=3\cdot10^{-4}$, $p_0=0.5$) keep directions that the flow and the race lose by $t_{\mathrm{end}}$; the amplitude of a lost direction dips by many orders of magnitude during the race, so round-off, which the race does not model, re-seeds it: the exact flow's smallest relative amplitude there is $\EtwoRoundMin$, and with a relative amplitude floor of $10^{-18}$ to $10^{-15}$ after every step it matches the measured survival in \EtwoRoundMatch{} of \EtwoRoundRuns{} runs (\texttt{results/checks/e2\_roundoff.json}).
The failed peak profile is not such an artifact: at $r=0.9$, $\lambda=3\cdot10^{-3}$ the exact flow keeps rank \EtwoMissFlowLong{} up to $t=\EtwoLongT$, so the race, not the measurement, misses it.
Continued to $t=\EtwoLongT$, \EtwoLongChanged{} runs gain directions (\EtwoLongSmallChanged{} of the \EtwoLongSmallRuns{} at $\lambda=3\cdot10^{-4}$, where $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ is capped) and \EtwoLongLost{} lose one; the pre-registered prediction is exact in \EtwoLongExactLong{} of runs against the long-horizon rank, and at $\lambda=3\cdot10^{-4}$ in \EtwoLongSmallExactLong{} against it and \EtwoLongSmallExactEnd{} against the rank at $t_{\mathrm{end}}$.
Scoring the same race without the cap on $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ (post hoc, nothing fitted) gives \EtwoLongUncappedExactLong{} against the long-horizon rank, so the cap, not the race, accounts for the difference.
Per family the race has rank error \EtwoBernMae{} (Bernoulli), \EtwoBlockMae{} (block) and \EtwoMultiMae{} (multiblock), and the per-frequency multiplicities match (\cref{fig:e2-app}); for non-wrapping blocks the circulant approximation has \EtwoNcCircMae{} against \EtwoNcMae{} for the general form.
SGD is less accurate with Bernoulli masks (\EtwoSgdBernMae{}) than with blocks (\EtwoSgdBlockMae{}).
The tanh encoder with Bernoulli masks converges in only \EtwoTanhBernConv{} of runs, its rank is still rising over the last quarter of training in \EtwoTanhBernRising{}, and its error to the race grows from \EtwoTanhBernMaeQuarter{} at $t_{\mathrm{end}}/4$ to \EtwoTanhBernMae{} at $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ (\texttt{results/checks/e2\_rank\_over\_time.json}, a post-hoc diagnostic): the nonlinearity keeps recruiting directions after the race, so the near-collapse premise does not hold there.
The two-layer encoder is predicted worse from its initial features (error \EtwoMlpMae{}) than by the linear race on the input statistics (\EtwoMlpLinMae{}), and with Bernoulli masks worse than the initial window (\EtwoMlpBernMae{} against \EtwoMlpBernWindowMae{}); with blocks it has \EtwoMlpBlockMae{}.
Retrospectively, after E2's result, a race on the statistics of its decaying first layer accounts for this miss (\cref{app:ext}, rung 2).

